Raise signals through the host in the ANDRUNA build.

inline_raise (used by abort and fdsan, among others) executes the
rt_tgsigqueueinfo system call with an inline syscall / svc instruction.
Andruna's guest bionic runs in a Windows process, where system calls are
made by calling the host's __andruna_syscall (aosp/bionic/README.md); the
instruction would enter the Windows kernel instead. Under ANDRUNA the
function uses syscall(), which goes through the host, as 32-bit x86 does.

diff --git a/libc/private/bionic_inline_raise.h b/libc/private/bionic_inline_raise.h
--- a/libc/private/bionic_inline_raise.h
+++ b/libc/private/bionic_inline_raise.h
@@ -48,7 +48,11 @@
   info.si_value.sival_ptr = value;
 
   long result;
-#if defined(__arm__)
+#if defined(ANDRUNA)
+  // System calls go through the host; syscall() sets errno itself.
+  (void)result;
+  return syscall(__NR_rt_tgsigqueueinfo, pid, tid, sig, &info);
+#elif defined(__arm__)
   register long r0 __asm__("r0") = pid;
   register long r1 __asm__("r1") = tid;
   register long r2 __asm__("r2") = sig;
